hi my name is Lamia user and this is my  MSX story when I first came to Stanford  I found out that I can volunteer to be  part of interdisciplinary classes  between the business school and  different other departments on campus  because I'm a computer scientist I  wanted to be part of the  interdisciplinary research between  business school and the computer science  department so I volunteered for this  class that was offered for the first  time at GSB on AI and machine learning  for business leaders in this class we  put together professors from the  business school and professors from the  computer science department in order to  bring together the knowledge of what  does it mean for AI at the discipline in  the business realm as well as at the  field at the research field one funny  story that came from this class is in  the first session when we were  introducing robotics and AI concepts the  first impression of the students was  robotics are going to take over the  world  it's a terminator kind of story it's  going to take over everything quickly  through the class we saw the change in  the perception of the students and they  are changing from the terminator story  to visiting the robotics lab here at  Stanford and seeing how the robotics  field is not as advanced as we thought  the most advanced robot that we have  here in Stanford which is one of the  most advanced in the world couldn't  climb stairs couldn't open doors and can  hardly communicate their emotions or  feelings the students came back and say  that's cute where did the Terminator  story come from and that was a change in  perception and more grounded truth into  where the field is whether from a  computer science point of view or from a  business point of view
 

